# Figma (Smart fleet)

## Always start with Smart orchestrator

For any Figma-linked ask (write to canvas **or** design→code), load **`figma-designer`** first
(`~/.cursor/skills/figma-designer/SKILL.md` + its `references/`). It maps the official
Figma Claude skill club and enforces hard gates. For **Club**
(`YR4B9skUnJe50tnfCyRwYo` / mount `club`), also load
`references/club-design-kit.md` (Design Kit V.2, IRANYekanXFaNum, seat/font limits).

Then load the official skill the orchestrator names (`figma-use`, `figma-generate-design`,
`figma-create-new-file`, and `figma-design-to-code` when installed).

## Branch A — work inside Figma (→ canvas)

Requirements → page, edit selection, empty state, new screen:

1. `figma-designer` → `figma-generate-design` + **`figma-use` before every `use_figma`**
2. Discover design system before mutating; wrapper first; one section per call; screenshot each section
3. MCP missing → `docs/cursor-mcp-pack.md` + Reload Window after `sync-cursor-mcp`

Fleet installs official trees under `~/.cursor/skills/`. `/add-plugin figma` is optional.

## Branch B — implement code from Figma (← canvas)

1. `figma-designer` → `figma-design-to-code` when present, else `get_design_context` with its rules
2. Treat MCP code as reference; reuse project components/tokens
3. Playwright check when feasible after meaningful UI changes

## Scope

Only when Figma links or explicit Figma design/canvas requests appear.
